<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Special containment procedures on top, description in the middle, and addendum at the bottom</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> There is a sheet of acid that exists that can make people hallucinate a whole new reality with a creature that will attack and kill them without mercy.<br />
.<br />
<strong>Central Narrative:</strong> When the participants of MKUltra were given tabs from this sheet of LSD they all began to overdose but when effects of a brutal assault started showing up on their bodies the foundation was asked to investigate. Using D-class personal to test the tabs ended up in several failures but eventually, enough survived to form a plausible conclusion. When asked about the drug's effects they each gave different statements about their trips which were nothing out of the ordinary for LSD side effects. One thing was constant for each of the descriptions though, in each trip, there was a purple-skinned humanoid creature that had dark burn-like marks on its body, a spherical head, and a permanent euphoric expression on its face, this creature then began to attack each of the D-Class personal until the psychedelic wore off. This creature was determined to be what caused the strange deaths of the MKUltra participants and the sheet of LSD was confiscated by the foundation.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention Grabber:</strong> This sheet of acid was a major reason that Project MKUltra was shut down but due to its anomalous nature it was confiscated by the foundation and the patient's deaths were covered up. Nobody but the person being attacked is able to see the creature, when the creature kills its victim all anybody can tell is that they died of an overdose but after a certain amount of time the effects of its grueling attack will be shown.</p>
<p><strong>Additional notes:</strong> Should I stick with this Idea or abandon it for a new one I want this to be a success</p>

