<p>Heyo, I'll take a look for you.<br />
Hmmmm I like the idea of an anomalous tab of LSD that lets you physically interact with hallucinations, but so far, this is a basic and slightly different form of 'Thing that kills you.'</p>
<p>Not much narrative happens aside from the monster killing you once you start tripping. It reminds me heavily of <a href="/scp-513">SCP-513</a>, in fact. However, even if something has already been done to death, it's what you do with it that can make it fresh all over again.</p>
<p>Even the blandest of anomalies (your anomaly kinda is, but is still usable) can be made interesting with a decent enough story. Like, this is lsd. It's a drug. Maybe a drug dealer made it to try to get back at someone? Just spitballing an idea here.</p>
<p>It doesn't even have to be a monster. You have a psychedelic drug (btw real life LSD doesn't make you hallucinate big scary things; you have really fast thoughts and, at most, see some pretty, swirling colors. But this is an SCP, so you can get away with it here.) that can let you interact with actual existing things. You can get a lot more creative than just a scary monster.</p>
<p>Anywho, I hope I helped and I bid you a lovely day. 👍👍👍</p>

