<p><em>Returned for followup crit; PM Request</em></p>
<p>Hmmmm it's definitely getting there, but it feels like the previous idea with a loosely tacked-on MK-Ultra plot point and for some reason, they just happen to think, 'hey, what about throwing our black belt martial artist D-class in there?'</p>
<p>There's also a matter of how you're going to present this in an article, so think on that as well.</p>
<p>I think I've done everything I can to offer advice. There's a fine line to be crossed that borders between giving guidance and straight up trying to turn someone else's idea into my own vision, and I do everything I can to avoid the latter. So, I've crit your idea twice and now I'll ask you to seek out other reviewers in <a href="/butterfly-squad-roster">the butterfly squad roster</a>. They're really good and really insightful reviewers on this page. Getting more perspectives on this idea is definitely my recommendation as of now.</p>
<p>You're definitely getting there, though, so don't give up!</p>
<p>If I were to offer some last minute suggestions before I head out, though&#8230;your sub reality part interests me more than the killer humanoid. There are endless killer humanoids out there. Do we really need another? That's not me dismissing this idea, mind you. Just challenging it.</p>
<p>Anywho, I hope I helped further and I bid you a good day. 👍</p>

